module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionCriteria.OpenCohomologyGlobalSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionCriteria.PrincipalDepthDimensionFiniteness
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.LocalCohomology.LocalCohomologyRangeFiniteLength

/-!
# Stacks 0DXU from the finite length of a local cohomology image

Fix an algebraization situation `S` whose ring `A` is Noetherian local with `𝔞 = 𝔪`, let
`I = (f)` be generated by a nonzerodivisor, and let `(ℱₙ)` be a coherent `I`-adic system on
`U = X ∖ V(𝔪)` each of whose terms is finite locally free over the infinitesimal neighbourhood it
is annihilated by — hypotheses (1), (3) and (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0DXU].  Writing
`Mₙ = H⁰(U, ℱₙ)`, this file assembles both conclusions of that tag from the single statement

  `∃ n, the image of H²_𝔪(Mₙ) ⟶ H²_𝔪(M₁) has finite length`

together with hypotheses (2) and (5).  It is the last link of the chain
`H²_𝔪(Mₙ) ⟶ H²_𝔪(M₁)` ⟶ `H¹(U, ℱₙ) ⟶ H¹(U, ℱ₁)` ⟶ condition (a) of [Stacks, Tag 0EHH] ⟶ the
tag, the first step of which is
`Stacks.Algebraization.isFiniteLength_range_openCohomology_of_isFiniteLength_range_localCohomology`
and the last
`Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_and_isCompletion_of_isFiniteLength_range`.

## Main results

* `isFiniteLength_range_localCohomologyDegreeFunctor_of_eq_maximalIdeal`: the two spellings of
  `H^q_𝔞(−)` on a map of modules, matched when `𝔞` is the maximal ideal: the degreewise functor
  `localCohomologyDegreeFunctor` and the homology of the coreflection that local duality is stated
  against.
* `canonicallyExtends_and_isCompletion_of_isFiniteLength_range_localCohomology`: both conclusions
  of [Stacks, Tag 0DXU] from hypotheses (1)–(5) together with the finite length of the image of
  `H²_𝔪(Mₙ) ⟶ H²_𝔪(M₁)` for some `n`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXG)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite IsLocalRing
open Stacks.RingTheory.PrincipalDivisorDepth

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

/-- **The two spellings of local cohomology at the maximal ideal, on a map of modules.**  The
functor `Stacks.Algebraization.localCohomologyDegreeFunctor A J hJ q` is, by definition, placing a
module in degree zero, applying the coreflection onto the objects with `J`-power-torsion
cohomology, and taking degree-`q` cohomology.  When `J` is the maximal ideal that is the composite
local duality is stated against, so the finite length of the image of a map transfers from one
spelling to the other. -/
theorem isFiniteLength_range_localCohomologyDegreeFunctor_of_eq_maximalIdeal
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (J : Ideal A) (hJ : J.FG) (hJm : J = maximalIdeal A) (q : ℤ)
    {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A} (φ : M ⟶ N)
    (h : IsFiniteLength A ↥(LinearMap.range
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) q).map
        ((Stacks.LocalCohomology.CechFormula.localCohomologyEndofunctor A
          (maximalIdeal A) (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)).map
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).map φ))).hom)) :
    IsFiniteLength A ↥(LinearMap.range
      ((localCohomologyDegreeFunctor A J hJ q).map φ).hom) := by
  subst hJm
  exact h

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0DXU] from the finite length of the image of `H²_𝔪(Mₙ) ⟶ H²_𝔪(M₁)`.**  Let `S`
be an algebraization situation whose ring `A` is local with `𝔞 = 𝔪` and which has a dualizing
complex — hypotheses (1) and (2) — let `I = (f)` be generated by a nonzerodivisor `f` —
hypothesis (3) — let every term of the system be finite locally free over the infinitesimal
neighbourhood it is annihilated by — hypothesis (4) — and let
`depth((A/fA)_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 1` for every `𝔭 ∈ V(f)` other than `𝔪` — hypothesis (5).  If for
some `n` the image of `H²_𝔪(Mₙ) ⟶ H²_𝔪(M₁)` has finite length, where `Mₙ = H⁰(U, ℱₙ)`, then
`(ℱₙ)` extends canonically to `X = Spec(A)`, and if `A` is `I`-adically complete then `(ℱₙ)` is
the completion of a coherent `𝒪_U`-module.

This is `Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_and_isCompletion_of_isFiniteLength_range` with
its condition-(a) input rewritten in the local cohomology spelling, by
`Stacks.Algebraization.isFiniteLength_range_openCohomology_of_isFiniteLength_range_localCohomology`
at `p = 1`.  It is the form in which the source's last step — local duality and Matlis duality
over the localizations `A_𝔮` at the primes `𝔮 ∈ V(f) ∖ {𝔪}` — delivers condition (a). -/
theorem canonicallyExtends_and_isCompletion_of_isFiniteLength_range_localCohomology
    (S : AlgebraizationSituation.{u}) [IsLocalRing S.A] (ha : S.a = maximalIdeal S.A)
    (F : Stacks.Coherent.CoherentAdicSystems (idealOnOpen S)) (f : S.A)
    (hI : S.I = Ideal.span {f}) (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors S.A)
    (hfree : IsFiniteLocallyFreeAdic (idealOnOpen S) F)
    (omega : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} S.A))
    (homega : Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex (A := S.A) (K := omega))
    (h5 : DepthDimOnDivisor f)
    (hrange : ∃ n : ℕ, IsFiniteLength S.A ↥(LinearMap.range
      ((localCohomologyDegreeFunctor S.A S.a (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing S.a)
            (((1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1)).map
        ((globalSectionsSystem S F).map (homOfLE (Nat.zero_le n)).op)).hom)) :
    CanonicallyExtends S F ∧
      (IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {f}) S.A →
        (completionFunctor S.U.toScheme (S.Yι.ker.comap S.U.ι)).essImage
          (kerComapSystem S F)) := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hrange
  exact canonicallyExtends_and_isCompletion_of_isFiniteLength_range S ha F f hI hf hfree
    omega homega h5
    ⟨n, isFiniteLength_range_openCohomology_of_isFiniteLength_range_localCohomology S F 1
      Nat.one_pos n hn⟩

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
